@{

	ViewData["Title"] = "Info";
}

<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/Info.css" />

<div class="pageToHide">
	<h1 class="fw-bold font-bungee text-center mb-5">INFO</h1>

	<div class="row justify-content-center pageToHide">
		<div class="col-11">
			<div id="infoBlock" class="text-center row justify-content-center glowingCard">
				<div class="col-11">
					<h2 class="font-robotoSlab fw-bold mt-4 mb-3">What is Gotcha?</h2>
					<p>Gotcha (also known as Assassin) is a social elimination game that’s all about stealth, creativity, and timing.
					<p>Everyone gets assigned a secret target from the player list.<p>
					<p>Your goal? “Eliminate” your target by completing your chosen style of challenge.</p>
					<p>It could be getting them to do something, or by catching them with a specific item.</p>
					<p>(This is customizable per game).</p>
					<p>Once you succeed, your target is out, and you take on their target.</p>
					<p>The game continues until only one player remains!<p>

						<h2 class="mt-4 mb-3 font-robotoSlab">What the app offers:</h2>
					<p>Gotcha is a great game to play with big groups, but setting it up can be quite a hassle.</p>
					<p>This app will remove the hassle of printing names and weapons and assigning them and will do it for you.</p>
					<p>Working with traditional paper is also quite limited.</p>
					<p>This app allows you to control what info people see to make it easier.</p>
					<p>(For example, you can turn on player images for groups where not everyone may know each other that well).</p>
					<p class="mb-4">The app also offers custom game modes that aren't possible with traditional paper.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>